{"id":11349,"date":"2024-05-05T10:30:26","date_gmt":"2024-05-05T17:30:26","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=11349"},"modified":"2024-06-04T10:48:58","modified_gmt":"2024-06-04T17:48:58","slug":"0-2-building-zumi","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-2-building-zumi\/","title":{"rendered":"0.2: Building Zumi"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214c23e809\" name=\"6a2214c23e809\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build Video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Zumi comes with a build guide in the box, but a video guide can come in handy as you follow along with the instructions. We recommend watching the video along with your build guide if you have never built a Zumi before. Once you&#8217;re done, go to the next step to check that Zumi is built correctly <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><b>before<\/b><\/span>\u00a0turning it on.[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1717022614867{background-color: #dbdbdb !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<strong>\u26a0\ufe0f Note: <\/strong>If you have a\u00a0<strong>black\u00a0<\/strong>Zumi board and not a <strong>red<\/strong> one, some steps in the video regarding the battery will look a little different. If this applies to you, take a look at an updated PDF below.[\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/youtu.be\/wzjaa0B7d-k&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<strong>PDF Version of Latest Zumi Manual<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/02\/buildmanual_v4.1_feb2023_spread.pdf\" class=\"pdfemb-viewer\" style=\"\" data-width=\"max\" data-height=\"max\" data-mobile-width=\"500\"  data-scrollbar=\"none\" data-download=\"on\" data-tracking=\"on\" data-newwindow=\"on\" data-pagetextbox=\"off\" data-scrolltotop=\"off\" data-startzoom=\"50\" data-startfpzoom=\"50\" data-toolbar=\"top\" data-toolbar-fixed=\"off\">buildmanual_v4.1_feb2023_spread<br\/><\/a>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214c23e969\" name=\"6a2214c23e969\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>OLED Check<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Wait! Before turning Zumi on, there will be a few things to double-check. Not doing so can damage your Zumi.<\/p>\n<p>First, the OLED cables should be connected correctly.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11450&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214c23e9c1\" name=\"6a2214c23e9c1\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>MicroSD Card<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The MicroSD should be inserted so that the gold part is facing up.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11451&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214c23ea0a\" name=\"6a2214c23ea0a\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>OLED and IR Sensors<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The OLED should not be cracked and the IR sensors should not be bent.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11452&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214c23ea4e\" name=\"6a2214c23ea4e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Pi0 pins<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The Pi0 pins should all be connected into the sockets. There should be no pins outside that are bent or exposed.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11453&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214c23eac2\" name=\"6a2214c23eac2\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Motors<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Check that the motors are oriented properly before putting on the shell. Motors that are placed backward may not spin.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11454&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214c23eb14\" name=\"6a2214c23eb14\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Pi Zero camera connection<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Verify that when connecting the ribbon cable to the Pi Zerp, the latch remained intact. Not connecting the camera properly may result in the camera not working.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11455&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214c23eb56\" name=\"6a2214c23eb56\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>``Sunny`` camera connector<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Before putting on the Zumi shell, check that the delicate connector is flush with the camera. If it looks lifted, gently push on the connector until you feel it click into place. If you have issues with your camera in the future, this is the first connector you should check. It can move around when packing up Zumi.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11456&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214c23ebbb\" name=\"6a2214c23ebbb\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Battery<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Last but certainly not least, check that the battery is connected in the right orientation before putting on the shell and turning on the switch. The red cable should be on the left and the black cable should be on the right.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;11457&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<strong>Connecting the battery<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>When connecting the battery, match the red wire with the (+) on the PCB and the black wire with the (-) on the PCB. Please do not connect the battery to any other connector on the board.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Removing the battery<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>If you need to remove the battery, grab the connector from the white plastic on the battery connector. A pair of pliers will do the job. Avoid tugging on the battery from the wires.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Low battery<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>When the battery is low, charge or power off Zumi. Allowing the battery to completely discharge will decrease the power of the battery over time.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Storing Zumi<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Always turn off Zumi when in storage. If you transport Zumi, it is also a good idea to disconnect the battery to avoid the switch turning itself on![\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2214c23ebfe\" name=\"6a2214c23ebfe\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 10<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Next steps<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]In the next step, you will power on Zumi and learn how to connect to the dashboard. Now that you&#8217;ve done your pre-power-on checks, let&#8217;s wake up Zumi![\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 11 Build Video [vc_column_text]Zumi comes with a build guide in the box, but a video guide can come in handy as you follow along with the instructions. We&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-2-building-zumi\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":2051,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":11339,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[13058,2135,2168,2177,2230],"class_list":["post-11349","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-assembly","lesson-tag-beginner","lesson-tag-build","lesson-tag-getting-started","lesson-tag-zumi","module-getting-started","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/11349","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":11,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/11349\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":11680,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/11349\/revisions\/11680"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/2051"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=11349"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=11349"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=11349"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}